{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.GCongr","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.smooth_period_excluded_as_magnitude","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.smooth_period_excluded_as_magnitude","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.lean#L79-L101","doc":"**Scope-(b): a smooth period cannot supply the factor-≈4 magnitude ratio.**\nIf a Lipschitz `P` on the anchor interval has variation budget\n`K·|qp − qm|/|P(qm)| < 1` — the regime of any `O(1)` geometric period over the\n`Δq ≈ 1.3e-8` anchor gap — then its ratio `r = P(qp)/P(qm)` satisfies `|r − 1| < 1`,\nso `|r| < 2` and it **cannot** equal the observed\n`|S_leak(proton)/S_leak(muon)| ≈ 4.075` (which has `|r| ≥ 2`). This is the SP1\nsmoothness wall for Bring-intrinsic periods: a smooth q₀-evaluated period is nearly\nconstant across the two anchors, so the factor-≈4 magnitude asymmetry cannot be a\nperiod ratio. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.smooth_ratio_near_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.smooth_ratio_near_one","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.lean#L66-L77","doc":"**Lipschitz ratio bound.** A function `P` whose variation over the anchor\ninterval is bounded by `K·|qp − qm|` has multiplicative ratio within\n`K·|qp − qm|/|P(qm)|` of `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.linear_ratio_slope_independent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.linear_ratio_slope_independent","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/SLeakMagnitudeOffsetRatio.lean#L55-L64","doc":"**Slope cancellation.** For the leading-order linearization of a function at a\nsimple zero `q*`, `S(q) = L·(q − q*)`, the ratio of two evaluations equals the ratio\nof their offsets from `q*`, *independently of the slope* `L ≠ 0`. Applied to the\nbar-odd residual `S_leak`, the observed `|S_leak(proton)/S_leak(muon)|` therefore\ncarries information about anchor placement relative to `q*` — not about the local\nslope, so no \"period value\" can be extracted from it. ","signatureChunk":0}]}